  "description": "A small MCP tool set for building a network topology: add-node,\n     add-link and find-path.\n\n     open-session mints a handle; every other tool takes it as its\n     'session' argument and checks that it names the record the call is\n     checked against (MCP 2026-07-28 has no protocol sessions).\n\n     Each tool is a grouping used twice: as its rpc's input (or output),\n     which compile_mcp.py turns into the tool's inputSchema (or\n     outputSchema), and as a recorded call in a session.\n\n     The grouping also carries the rules, so one rule checks a call in both\n     places. Rules that need earlier calls read them from the session with\n     an absolute path, /topo:session/topo:call, and keep only calls with a\n     smaller id than this one:\n\n       [not(current()/../../../id) or id < current()/../../../id]\n\n     For a recorded call, current()/../../../id is the call's own id. When\n     an rpc input is validated with the session as context, the input's\n     parameters sit under the operation node, directly below the root\n     (RFC 7950, section 6.4.1), so that path selects nothing and every\n     recorded call counts as earlier. A link may therefore only join nodes\n     that an earlier successful call created, whether the link is a request\n     arriving now or a line in the record.\n     SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT",
  "$defs": {
